-- check/bad: §10.5. One variable carries one constraint per method name
-- (§6.1 invariant 3), so two uses of `x.render` have to agree and these do
-- not — the first takes one argument, the second two. This is Roc's rank-2
-- limitation reproduced deliberately; §11 records that the fix is stretch
-- item 1. The primary span is the YOUNGER use, at 10:21, and the older one
-- is quoted in the prose.
--
-- The arity is what makes the two disagree AT the method node. §10.5's own
-- example, `( x.render 1, x.render "two" )`, disagrees one step later — the
-- second call's argument variable is still fresh when its method node is
-- solved, so the two method types unify and `"two"` then meets `number` —
-- and gets `type_mismatch` at the argument instead, which is a better span
-- and a different code.
pub widen x =
    ( x.render 1, x.render 1 2 )
